keywords:
  - interpretability
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - sparse autoencoder
  - activation steering
  - attention visualization
  - agent observability
  - local-first
abstract: >-
  ModelMRI is an open-source, local-first inspector for AI models and agents.
  It renders per-layer, per-head attention from a live forward pass, decomposes
  the residual stream with sparse autoencoders, applies causal steering along a
  chosen feature direction, visualises the attention of vision-language-action
  robot policies, and records agent runs as inspectable traces through a
  zero-dependency recorder.
